Foveated single layer (`[ofxr] foveated_single_layer`, on unless 0, live; `foveated_single_layer_scale`, 25-100 %
of the runtime's recommended view size, default 100, start only). With foveated frame generation Quad Views
(dcsvr_two_layers) hands over a periphery and a focus projection layer per eye and each is synthesized on its own.
Handed to the runtime as two layers, Pimax composes them with per-layer distortion: its chromatic aberration
correction samples red and blue across the focus layer's border (the orange/red line around the focus area, flights
of 2026-11-22) and, wherever the focus alpha is below 1 (0031's ramp), it shows its own periphery under the focus,
which on some frames is not the one the focus was composed against (the flickering focus rectangle in the right eye,
2026-11-23). The presenter now composes every fresh submission's two layers into one image per eye before it goes
down (D3D12FoveatedComposer, src/d3d12/foveated_compose.hlsl: the runtime's blend on the stored values, the focus
colour over the periphery by the focus layer's alpha, at the periphery's field of view and pose), while the frame's
images are still the layer's (their release follows), and the frame names that image as ONE opaque projection layer.
Real and generated frames alike; a repeat names the composed swapchain again, which shows the image of the frame it
repeats (every repeat is of the last fresh submission). One composed swapchain per session (array of the views, the
periphery's format), made on first use; the frame path defers the private images' release to the hand-over on a
D3D12 binding without the layer's own queue too while the key is on. Flight log: foveated_mode result=4 (state),
5 (swapchain made), 6 (GPU time every 900 compositions), live_settings result=4 (the key followed live).
Tests: xrfg_foveated_composer_tests (WARP: both eyes, the three alpha modes, sub-images, a rotated focus view, typed
sRGB, a ring of frames, each against a CPU reference of the runtime's blend; bench label: GPU time at a Crystal
Super's sizes), xrfg_layer_two_layers_deep_hold_composed_{off,2x,3x,auto,opaque} (the fake runtime checks every
composed frame: one layer without blend flags on the composed swapchain's two slices, alpha 255); the other
two-layer tests run with the key off (unchanged). tests/quadviews-composition checks the shader against Quad Views'
own composition.

